                <pb facs="0576" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 12344/18–19.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Secretary of Legation
                        Gibson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 1, dated the 18th ultimo, reporting the action taken by you on
                    instruction No. 3, of October 15 last, in which you were directed to ascertain
                    whether the Honduranean Government will, as an act of courtesy, and in
                    anticipation of the extradition treaty for which negotiations are now pending,
                    grant the extradition of William Adler, William H. Simmons, and John Ripplinger
                    to the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that your course in the matter is approved by the
                    department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
